138
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:22,999
attention and vigilance. This is what he is sharing through this testimony.

139
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:30,999
His son’s desire to study Computer Science in B.Tech, and the obstacles that arose from the moment he started preparing for the entrance exam,

140
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:37,999
each hindrance came as a challenge to even write the exam. Mother gives the message to handle these obstacles.

141
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:45,999
He asks if there is any law anywhere that says a blind person cannot study Computer Science.

142
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:53,999
Since no such law exists, permission is granted to write the exam. Even when the rank list arrives,

143
00:19:54,000 --> 00:20:01,999
there are obstacles—problems arise in bringing a scribe. When it was time to bring a scribe to the school,

144
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:11,999
a woman entered, smelling of jasmine, and intervened in the matter. Who she was cannot be seen; we do not know,

145
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,999
but we can sense it. It was Mother’s presence, like the fragrance of jasmine, a special intervention he recognizes.

146
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:27,999
He says, every time, “I have no one with me. Only Mother, only Jesus. So at the most difficult times,

147
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:36,999
when I have no one to plead for me, Mother must be there to intercede.”

148
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:44,999
That is how one person came, entered, presented the matter, motivated the principal to write the statement of truth, and then left.

149
00:20:45,000 --> 00:21:00,999
Both he and his son have limited or no sight, but the scribe and the scribe’s guardians can see.

150
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:08,999
They watched, but could not see who this person was. They could not thank them. That is what he is saying.

151
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:17,999
He received Mother’s special intervention there. Even when his son received college admission, obstacles arose.

152
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:33,999
Only crises arise in this domain, but never once did Mother’s covenant fail to bring success in life. The faith in this hope is unwavering.

153
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:42,999
Likewise, there is no doubt that Mother takes on the burdens, eases them, makes life manageable, and protects it.

154
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:55,999
Fully surrendering, he recites the prayer of faith, the apparition prayers, holding the covenant medal tightly in hand, intervening for this intention.

155
00:21:56,000 --> 00:22:05,999
He says those who had denied him were granted admission to a nearby college, opening the path for studies.

156
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:14,999
Then another crisis arose: a boil grew on his navel, causing intense pain.

157
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:22,999
Only two or three days were left before college. At that time, a matter arose at home testing faith: his partner’s lack of belief.

158
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:29,999
Nevertheless, he says it is not about how others perceive faith; when he took the covenant and lived with complete trust in Mother,

159
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:44,999
if he mentioned something to her, Mother would hear it. If he indicated a matter, Mother would observe it.

160
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:55,999
In insignificant moments, Mother can make even the greatest issue for the son turn into a miraculous comfort and experience. That is why he says,

161
00:22:56,000 --> 00:23:06,999
that evening he twice drew the cross on a basket, applied the holy oil, recited the prayer of faith, prayed seven times, thirty-three times.

162
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:12,999
All these prayers he followed as instructed. The next morning, he was ready to go to the hospital,

163
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:17,999
though by his wife’s insistence, he was going to show the boil that no longer existed.

164
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:26,999
He is testifying at the altar about complete physical health. Mother intervenes in any domain of life,

165
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:34,999
and if called with a heartfelt request, she will come alongside and provide solutions and guidance to move forward.

166
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:51,999
He shares that insight. The phrase that struck him most: he cannot perform mercy or mission work fully due to the limitation of sight.

167
00:23:52,000 --> 00:24:05,999
He renewed the covenant twice and said that he could now distribute newspapers. Many of us carry a bundle, but we cannot distribute it in one month.

168
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:14,999
He says with pain, “Because of this limitation, I am unable to do much.”

169
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:22,999
Even though he cannot do much, he could distribute ten bundles of newspapers. This shows his heart: even within his limitations,

170
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:29,999
when life is aligned with Mother’s vow, which bears witness to Jesus, the covenant itself becomes a blessing in life.

171
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:35,999
He shared with us the mission he joyfully carries out despite these limitations.

172
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:44,999
Dear ones, this family—the father and son—stand at this altar as witnesses to the living presence of God and the apparition of the Holy Mother.

173
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:52,999
They give thanks for the great divine experiences they received, and we, too, may ask that Jesus’s intervention flow through Mother into our lives.

174
00:24:53,000 --> 00:25:06,999
Let us pray and clap our hands in offering this testimony, lifting every burden in devotion.

175
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:15,999
Such extraordinary divine experiences—if you have not yet subscribed to this YouTube channel, do so now.

